-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Assets that are NOT part of this distribution
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The default "aphesis" theme can use the aphes.ist identity assets: the
Aphesis Script typeface, the phi mark and the wordmark. They are not included
in this repository or in builds made from it, and they are not covered by the
Apache License. They are fetched at install time into
ui/theme/themes/aphesis/assets/ by ui/theme/scripts/fetch-aphesis-assets.mjs.

  Aphesis Script  to be licensed by its author under the SIL Open Font
                  License 1.1 with the Reserved Font Name "Aphesis Script";
                  until that licence is published it is all rights reserved
                  and must not be redistributed.
  phi mark and    trademarks of the owner of aphes.ist. The Apache License
  wordmark        grants no trademark rights (section 6).

Without them the theme falls back to Special Elite and a placeholder stipple
mark (ui/theme/marks/), both Apache-2.0. Forks should set their own mark and
display face. Details: ui/theme/themes/aphesis/assets/NOTICE.md.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Model weights and data
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No model weights are included. With the default "local" embedding feature,
the ONNX Runtime library is downloaded when the crate is built and the
embedding model (intfloat/multilingual-e5-small, MIT) is downloaded on first
use into the user's cache directory, under their own licences.

The demo brain is not included. The lab builds it on the user's machine from
texts that are in the public domain in the United States and Brazil
(lab/README.md).
